{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes","id":198676,"title":"Kindred and lasting physical changes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-16T01:14:50-07:00","id":198676,"title":"Kindred and lasting physical changes","content":"I watched today last <i>True Blood</i> episode, and seeing how Erick and Pam change on the last three decades ( from 1980's to 2010's ) it got me thinking - in original <b>Requiem</b> changes like hair style or nail length needed to be repeated with each night, after Embrace ( I could suppose that defloration also, like with Jessica in series ). It is in spirit of Ann Rice's <i>Vampire Chronicles</i> saga, that was one of main inspirations for game.<br /> <br /> But with the take on Kindred being more and more in tune with modern times, weren't developers change this with <b>Blood and Smoke</b>. If not, would rules like spending Willpower Dot for letting body to take new changes in appearance be good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T01:36:13-07:00","id":198695,"title":"","content":"Both baseline Requiem (p. 175) and Blood &amp; Smoke (p. 91) include rules for using Willpower to make alterations permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T02:23:15-07:00","id":198746,"title":"","content":"If I read <b>Blood and Smoke</b> rules correctly, it's only Willpower Point for one night, and later change is permanent, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T06:18:32-07:00","id":198882,"title":"","content":"One willpower point to make an alteration permanent, like tattoos, piercings and haircuts, i believe. You might want to be careful with the last one because they can always be cut shorter but will never grow back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T07:46:41-07:00","id":198940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=198882#post198882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One willpower point to make an alteration permanent, like tattoos, piercings and haircuts, i believe. You might want to be careful with the last one because they can always be cut shorter but will never grow back.</div> </div> </div> </div> If they're willing to blow the vitae to keep Blush of Life active night after night, and spend willpower they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:06:07-07:00","id":198954,"title":"","content":"I zay it's a bit stupid - it shouldbe permanent change. Or no change at all. Thing is - what with longer hair or nails? They can't be made LONGER?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:07:11-07:00","id":198957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=198954#post198954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I zay it's a bit stupid - it shouldbe permanent change. Or no change at all. Thing is - what with longer hair or nails? They can't be made LONGER?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, with blush of life active - they grow. However each night, during the Cleansing your body reverts back to it's original form, unless you spend willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T11:45:26-07:00","id":199133,"title":"","content":"Same thing with a guy who wants to look buff, when he was skinny when Embraced. He'd need to train with the Blush of Life active, and then spend willpower to &quot;store&quot; the effects of his training upon his body. It'd take a long time, but then, he -has- a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T12:35:39-07:00","id":199153,"title":"","content":"A lot of characters I've played shave their heads, spend Willpower to make the change permanent, and just wear wigs. As for fingernails, isn't that what Protean is for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T12:41:22-07:00","id":199159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=199133#post199133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same thing with a guy who wants to look buff, when he was skinny when Embraced. He'd need to train with the Blush of Life active, and then spend willpower to &quot;store&quot; the effects of his training upon his body. It'd take a long time, but then, he -has- a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could see this, but something like &quot;you tried it two weeks now. With enough power of your will, you can make it permanent&quot; and let player spend Willpower DOT on this. Vampires should be static, but not as much - they change hairs, nails and piercings from time to time. Other way elders would end bald after few centuries of era adjustments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> After Willpower DOT spend, no more points in use.<br /> <br /> And very interesting thing with Protean - so, basically, Gangrels are only Clan that can grow longer hair from the start? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T12:55:00-07:00","id":199181,"title":"","content":"Or they simply shave their head every night before going out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T15:08:16-07:00","id":199315,"title":"","content":"Hmm, if a vampire can have make-up automatically applied each night if that's how they got Embraced, could they do similar things with wigs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:30:42-07:00","id":199392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=199315#post199315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, if a vampire can have make-up automatically applied each night if that's how they got Embraced, could they do similar things with wigs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, when was that ever the case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:50:03-07:00","id":199407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=199315#post199315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, if a vampire can have make-up automatically applied each night if that's how they got Embraced, could they do similar things with wigs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I made this assumption a little while go, but felt it was a bit silly once I thought about it more. Like in the case of what makes makeup distinctive from other objects people place on their person, like hair dye or piercings. In other words, do I &quot;regenerate&quot; my piercings if I lose them at night?<br /> <br /> That seems sort of silly to me, and makeup is just a grouping of creams and dusts and other materials coated on your person, so I don't see why they'd come back anymore than the aforementioned magical brow piercing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T18:50:29-07:00","id":199518,"title":"","content":"Would Hair extensions fall out every day? Lets Look at how women use many many many!!!! Things to give them the apperance they want my. Ex she had a pixie cut, and her staff Sgt kept giving her shit so she just put in extensions. we forget humans have worked for freken eternity to match them selves to the beauty of the time/culture/sub-culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1163-mr-ink","name":"MR.Ink","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T19:13:12-07:00","id":199550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=199407#post199407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made this assumption a little while go, but felt it was a bit silly once I thought about it more. Like in the case of what makes makeup distinctive from other objects people place on their person, like hair dye or piercings. In other words, do I &quot;regenerate&quot; my piercings if I lose them at night?<br /> <br /> That seems sort of silly to me, and makeup is just a grouping of creams and dusts and other materials coated on your person, so I don't see why they'd come back anymore than the aforementioned magical brow piercing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, maybe not. Just something my first storyteller was quite sure about that stuck in my assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:36:48-07:00","id":199694,"title":"","content":"Basically, &quot;guys who don't know how make-up works&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's a merit in Clanbook Mekhet, Doll Face, that lets them have hair and make-up done perfectly upon waking each night, but as they lose Humanity they look more like mannequins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T04:05:58-07:00","id":199881,"title":"","content":"If you're suggesting that men are so ignorant of make-up and stupid in general that they don't even realize it's layers upon the skin, then I think that's rude, sexist and uncalled for in the present discussion. Seeing as there's supernatural powers at work and some fiction does have vampires wake fully groomed, you don't have to be particularly stupid to make such an assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T06:40:53-07:00","id":199958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=199881#post199881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're suggesting that men are so ignorant of make-up and stupid in general that they don't even realize it's layers upon the skin, then I think that's rude, sexist and uncalled for in the present discussion. Seeing as there's supernatural powers at work and some fiction does have vampires wake fully groomed, you don't have to be particularly stupid to make such an assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div> Technically it's not sexist, it's just sexually prejudiced, but that's a pretty semantic difference. At any rate, I agree it's silly to assume men don't know how makeup works - working in theater, I've known plenty of men who are more knowledgable about makeup and better at applying it than a lot of women I kmow. Anyway, I don't think it makes any sense for vampires to awaken fully made up each night. Apart from makeup not being an actual part of their actual bodies, it kind of breaks conservation of matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:15:10-07:00","id":200079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MR.Ink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=199518#post199518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Hair extensions fall out every day? Lets Look at how women use many many many!!!! Things to give them the apperance they want my. Ex she had a pixie cut, and her staff Sgt kept giving her shit so she just put in extensions. we forget humans have worked for freken eternity to match them selves to the beauty of the time/culture/sub-culture.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think they'd fall out any more than the cleansing would automatically divest you of your clothing each time. Tattoos are different since they essentially damage your skin, and cutting your hair damages your hair. Hence they repair/disappear every day sleep unless you will them not to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T11:34:32-07:00","id":200278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=199958#post199958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Technically it's not sexist, it's just sexually prejudiced, but that's a pretty semantic difference. At any rate, I agree it's silly to assume men don't know how makeup works - working in theater, I've known plenty of men who are more knowledgable about makeup and better at applying it than a lot of women I kmow. Anyway, I don't think it makes any sense for vampires to awaken fully made up each night. Apart from makeup not being an actual part of their actual bodies, it kind of breaks conservation of matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, once it was pointed out I do agree, it was just a sort of &quot;never really stopped to actually think it through&quot; sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T13:00:02-07:00","id":200323,"title":"","content":"Okay so, the kindred body wants nothing more than to return to the state of when if was embraced. Cuts heal, holes are grown over (ie. piercings. Although whether or not they actually cause the piercing to fall out is another matter. I would imagine that if you go to sleep with any piercings, they get stuck in your skin and the only way to remove them would be by tearing them out), any lost hair grows back, etc. But what about things on your skin? Like Leetsepeak said, you don't lose your clothes when you go to sleep. Not going to wake up and find your satin pajama's have been magically torn from your body. So would your make-up just stay on your skin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T13:45:43-07:00","id":200364,"title":"","content":"Yes, makeup would stay on your skin just as it would on a mortal, barring that your skin exudes no greases or sweat as a Vampire so perhaps slightly better even. Same goes naturally for clothes. As for piercings taken I would rule that they are generally rejected from your body as it heals, since that's what even a normal body tries to achieve on any foreign objects in it, failing that it heals around it and seeks to encapsulate it, and we are talking about supernatural healing that tends to bleed the ink out of your skin in case of Tattoos, instead of just healing.<br /> <br /> Personally I kinda dislike the whole burn WP to change what you look like. I just find it stretching that thin line of disbelief towards breaking point. Cause how do you justify it in character? You just really, really, really want your hair to stay this way? So generally in my games your stuck as you were embraced and just have to deal with it. And it is doable, like shaving your head each night or having it cut each night etc, it's not like it makes it impossible for elders to blend in, just harder.<br /> <br /> If you permanently want to change how you look it should require a bit more supernatural mojo than just wishing for it really hard, but that's just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T13:58:47-07:00","id":200389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=200364#post200364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally I kinda dislike the whole burn WP to change what you look like. I just find it stretching that thin line of disbelief towards breaking point. Cause how do you justify it in character? You just really, really, really want your hair to stay this way? So generally in my games your stuck as you were embraced and just have to deal with it. And it is doable, like shaving your head each night or having it cut each night etc, it's not like it makes it impossible for elders to blend in, just harder. If you permanently want to change how you look it should require a bit more supernatural mojo than just wishing for it really hard, but that's just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think making it completely inaccessible would be a bit extreme, but it's been discussed in the books that the expenditure of willpower to maintain an alteration to your body isn't no casual thing. Like any time you spend willpower, it's about putting your all into it, fighting the manifestation of the curse for agency over your body. Narratively it's not something done too lightly even if it's super well known by Kindred, because people aren't used to putting their will into something like resisting a supernatural change like that. I recall how one of the line's previous books made a point of how piercings and other bodymods are a status symbol that show you have the will and the desire to assert change over what is a typically static Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T14:00:37-07:00","id":200391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=200364#post200364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, makeup would stay on your skin just as it would on a mortal, barring that your skin exudes no greases or sweat as a Vampire so perhaps slightly better even. Same goes naturally for clothes. As for piercings taken I would rule that they are generally rejected from your body as it heals, since that's what even a normal body tries to achieve on any foreign objects in it, failing that it heals around it and seeks to encapsulate it, and we are talking about supernatural healing that tends to bleed the ink out of your skin in case of Tattoos, instead of just healing. Personally I kinda dislike the whole burn WP to change what you look like. I just find it stretching that thin line of disbelief towards breaking point. Cause how do you justify it in character? You just really, really, really want your hair to stay this way? So generally in my games your stuck as you were embraced and just have to deal with it. And it is doable, like shaving your head each night or having it cut each night etc, it's not like it makes it impossible for elders to blend in, just harder. If you permanently want to change how you look it should require a bit more supernatural mojo than just wishing for it really hard, but that's just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Ordo clan book has a lot of info on the in-narrative processes a Vampire must go through to make physical changes &quot;stick&quot;&quot;. The Willpower is just a mechanical representation of the fact that it takes a great effort, but really you should have to actually do something in character. Just like you can't necessarily buy a Merit just because you have the xp for it unless you've earned it in character, you can't necessarily make a change permanent just because you have a point of Willpower to spare unless you've worked on it in character. Maybe you use meditation to access your subconscious and hold off your natural instinct to heal. Maybe you tear your own skin down to the bone and painstakingly regrow and tattoo one layer at a time. Maybe you create some kind of chemical compound that halts your regenerative processes and apply it to the area you want to pierce before doing so. As with developing Coils, the exact process will vary from one Kindred to the next, but the results are the same - you exert a great force of personal will towards maintaining a post-embrace change to your body (whatever that looks like for your character), spend a point of Willpower, and that day your Vitae does not reverse that change while you sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T14:06:16-07:00","id":200393,"title":"","content":"It's the same thing as spending willpower to avoid healing too grievous wound during sleep, avoiding the risk to remain with no blood to wake up. You spend willpower to make a wound permanent untill you have the blood to heal it back (otherwise it autonomously heals as you sleep). Basically, vampires physical changes are actually treated as wounds by the vampire body and they &quot;heal back&quot; with the automatic blood point spent to wake up. This could actually mean you can willingly go back on every change you made by spending point to heal them back just as you do with normal wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T14:45:45-07:00","id":200412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=199407#post199407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made this assumption a little while go, but felt it was a bit silly once I thought about it more. Like in the case of what makes makeup distinctive from other objects people place on their person, like hair dye or piercings. In other words, do I &quot;regenerate&quot; my piercings if I lose them at night?<br /> <br /> That seems sort of silly to me, and makeup is just a grouping of creams and dusts and other materials coated on your person, so I don't see why they'd come back anymore than the aforementioned magical brow piercing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The piercing would remain (as it was in pre-embrace), even if the hardware were ripped out. Thus, you just put in new hardware. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T16:23:37-07:00","id":200499,"title":"","content":"Man, I'm showing my &quot;I don't have piercings&quot; card right now. I meant the jewelry you put in the piercing, i.e. regenerating the nose ring as opposed to the hole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T06:45:51-07:00","id":201048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cause how do you justify it in character? You just really, really, really want your hair to stay this way? </div> </div> </div>I could see it from a breaking point. Did something horrible, lost some humanity, you start to feel that what you see in the mirror is a lie. That person doesn't exist anymore. So you go and change it. Kind of like a mini mid-life crisis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T07:40:14-07:00","id":201075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=200499#post200499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I'm showing my &quot;I don't have piercings&quot; card right now. I meant the jewelry you put in the piercing, i.e. regenerating the nose ring as opposed to the hole.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ahh... Of course. And of course the Hardware would not regenerate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T11:31:55-07:00","id":201314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=200393#post200393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the same thing as spending willpower to avoid healing too grievous wound during sleep, avoiding the risk to remain with no blood to wake up. You spend willpower to make a wound permanent untill you have the blood to heal it back (otherwise it autonomously heals as you sleep). Basically, vampires physical changes are actually treated as wounds by the vampire body and they &quot;heal back&quot; with the automatic blood point spent to wake up. This could actually mean you can willingly go back on every change you made by spending point to heal them back just as you do with normal wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this interpretation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T11:55:51-07:00","id":201323,"title":"","content":"I believe that TittoPaolo's explanation is the one that reflects Blood &amp; Smoke's version of making this change. I just think if you feel that it isn't enough that one could use the strong narrative component presented in <i>Ordo Dracul</i> to make it less of a casual thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T14:13:52-07:00","id":604165,"title":"","content":"I think I stick with Willpower DOT for larger changes ( change of hair, maybe permanent makeups ) instead of WP point. I was shocked and thrilled for Ann Rice's version from <i>Vampire Chronicles</i> of &quot;vampires does not change&quot;. On the other hand I know sometimes character need to evolve in game setting. Willpower DOT is also nice middle point for this - very high price for very large life alteration. Also, <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b> paragraph is vague enough to sustain this interpretation<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Blood &amp; Smoke on the Cleansing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, Kindred force other marks to remain. For example, vampires often keep scars, tattoos, and piercings for spiritual reasons or just to fit in with the flock. Many Kindred remove long hair, in favor of wigs or cleaner, more modern styles. The vampire spends Willpower to fight the healing process while she sleeps. After a day\u2019s rest, any damage heals as normal, but her body remains changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower Points maybe would do for piercing and exercises, but larger changes need larger commitment - in form of Willpower Dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-26-2015, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T14:55:24-07:00","id":604195,"title":"","content":"A Willpower dot has always seemed to me like an incredibly steep tax just for a player to make a purely cosmetic change to their character. At that point, you might as well just say it's impossible to make permanent physical changes, because who in their right minds would willingly decrease their maximum capacity for such an important character resource just so they can describe their character with shorter hair? All this accomplishes is forcing players to bend over backwards to justify the appearance they want their character to have as part of their background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T15:04:50-07:00","id":604200,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I really think the narrative idea of it being difficult accomplishes the goal of making there be a barrier without that barrier being so steep that it isn't reasonable to expect someone to make that decision mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T23:16:01-07:00","id":604535,"title":"","content":"I feel like whenever these discussion come up we go to a little white room and forget some serious considerations. Let us assume that Blush of Life allows for hair, fingernails, muscle development, and even aging (as in wrinkles and gray hair, not physical development) at the normal rate while the effect is on. It would take hundreds of vitae and willpower points to grow hair, fingernails or &quot;get toned&quot;. It would take thousands for your hair to grow long. Aging a decade would be many thousands. Even in the best case scenario, this would take about twice as long. Generally, it would take &quot;forever.&quot; All of this would occur in the background. Unless the chronicle has serious time skipping, then these issues don't really come up.<br /> <br /> If there is lots of time skipping (or long periods of time) then you can figure out based on a character's resources roughly how long it should take to reach the desired effect and assume it happens. The huge amount of character resources expended and the time it took illustrate just how difficult it is for a vampire to change from the point of Embrace. I'm in the group that says it should only take a few vitae and willpower to revert back to the state at embrace no matter what physical changes have occurred, short of final death. Those two together make vampires practically, as opposed to completely, as unchanging as just saying you can't change at all.<br /> <br /> False nails, wigs, and makeup are the way a vampire is going to go if they want to change their appearance with any regularity. If it is just once every 50 years to keep up with the times then I say let it happen. The movie Dracula from the 90's has him go from young to old and back to young again after becoming a vampire. It isn't the only point of reference for this type of thing occurring either. There is no harm in allowing &quot;permanent&quot; changes to be undone or &quot;impermanent&quot; physical traits to change over long periods of time. It fits with the general idea of a vampire doesn't appear to vary once embraced. It would only be niche cases where that level of stuff is occurring. Wigs and makeup would be the norm.<br /> <br /> I would keep &quot;Claudia's curse&quot; by not allowing physical maturity without magic. Even Blush of Life doesn't mean a vampire suddenly requires food again. There would be no basis for the body to mature. Aging is a different process. A child that is embraced may appear to grow older over time, but they would appear as an old person that never actually grew up into an adult which happens.<br /> <br /> This is just a game and we probably think way too hard about some of these things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T03:48:28-07:00","id":604575,"title":"","content":"This is why the ordo dracul have a rep as being the ones who can do it. Coil of the Ascendant, second dot. 24/7 blush of life party time, just one vitae per day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T15:07:32-07:00","id":605061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=604575#post604575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why the ordo dracul have a rep as being the ones who can do it. Coil of the Ascendant, second dot. 24/7 blush of life party time, just one vitae per day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but for how long? Finger nails grow 3mm per month and hair is about 0.5 inches per month. I say twice as long for the dragons compared to mortals because I assume they won't focus their entire &quot;lives&quot; on the endeavor. If they do then that is a whole other level of dedication to the process. 1 vitae and willpower a day for months is no small thing. Blood Sorcery should be able to do similar things so seemingly permanent transformations should be something that is known to be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T15:59:51-07:00","id":605091,"title":"","content":"The transformations revert when they sleep. A dragon with that coil never has to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T16:49:07-07:00","id":605122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=605091#post605091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The transformations revert when they sleep. A dragon with that coil never has to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a niche loophole and so I won't accept it unless specifically stated to be true. They still burn a vitae as if they slept and woke up, so unless something requires &quot;a full day of sleep&quot; it should happen at some point during the day whether the vampire sleeps or not. We're talking about something a vampire is supposed to be required to use a great effort of will to avoid it from happening. I don't think it is right to bypass it because writers don't specify every single possible niche case. If you want it to work that way then you should probably be using willpower dots to make it happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T19:04:04-07:00","id":605181,"title":"","content":"Well typically, it seems to be that you are stuck in the state you were in just before your embrace. I can't remember where, but I think I read something that said a vampire can will their vitae to heal pre-existing conditions, but these conditions revert themselves while they sleep the day away. For example, an amputee who becomes a vampire could use their vitae to grow back the limbs they lost for the night, but they would fall off again during the day and they'd have to do it again when they woke up.<br /> <br /> The prince of New Orleans in the 1st edition book is described as needing to spend the first 2 hours of every night cleaning himself up because he was embraced in a disheveled state and didn't have time to make himself more presentable.<br /> <br /> <br /> It also mentions that when left to their privacy, elders prefer to surround themselves with things from their era. Even when in public, the elders are known to dress in clothing that seems decades out of date with the rest of the public, because they don't adapt well to the times. Some of them prefer to use written messages because they don't understand how email works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The thing is; how can vampires claim to be immortal or have eternal youth if their body is allowed to undergo permanent changes or signs of aging? The answer is that they can't. If your body can age, you don't have eternal youth. If your body can be permanently transfigured, you're not immortal.<br /> <br /> If you want vampires who can change their appearance, I'd suggest reading a bit of the Cirque du Freak series (not that god awful movie they made). For every 10 years, the vampires age by 1, unless you're a half vampire (partially embraced) in which case you age 1 year for every 5. One of the oldest vampires in the world is only about 700 to 800 years old, which makes him between the physical ages of 70 to 80.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-27-2015, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T00:11:11-07:00","id":605353,"title":"","content":"Continuing to age after the embrace is actually the bloodline weakness for the seriously creepy Oberloch bloodline. They're still as immortal as any of the Kindred, however; &quot;Old Alice,&quot; the matriarch of the insular lineage, is rumored to be somewhere on the order of 150 and 200 years old, and looks every day of her age.<br /> <br /> As for the static nature of Vampires, second edition has departed a bit from first in that it places more emphasis on vampires being well adapted to their condition. On the one hand, vampires see well in the dark (which is something I always house ruled in <i>Masquerade</i> and <i>Requiem</i> 1e anyway; I'm not sure how creatures that burn in the sun and are afraid of fire are supposed to have survived most of human history without really good night vision), and can hear heartbeats and smell blood from afar, and can even track prey by scent if they're bleeding.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, vampires are also well adapted to blend into human society. The lost visage is a much more subtle effect than in 1e; instead of having weird reflections and showing up blurry on film (which is far more of a liability than a boon in terms of hiding out), they just have a preternatural combination of instinct and blind luck that ensures that their image is always somehow concealed. In addition, the strange dreams vampires suffer during torpor have an adaptive function, keeping the mind sort of plastic so that awakening elders are surprisingly quick to adapt to the changed circumstances they wake up to.<br /> <br /> I imagine that many elders might still find it comforting to surround themselves with the trappings of their mortal life in private - some of these trappings might even be touchstones - but an elder who entered torpor in 1815 will usually be fairly quick to figure out cellphones and the internet when he wakes up in 2015... or at least, to figure them out well enough that he doesn't immediately stand out as strangely inept and out-of-touch.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Kindred body is receptive to minor cosmetic changes. A vampire embraced in the Danelaw in the 9th century might have been quite the lady's man in his time with his long, bleached hair and beard, but he'd have a much harder time hunting in 19th century England if he couldn't adopt a more &quot;conservative&quot; hairstyle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-28-2015, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T02:53:56-07:00","id":605429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=605122#post605122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a niche loophole </div> </div> </div> </div>Well of course it is. This is the Ordo Dracul we're talking about here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T05:57:58-07:00","id":605518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=604165#post604165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I stick with Willpower DOT for larger changes ( change of hair, maybe permanent makeups ) instead of WP point. I was shocked and thrilled for Ann Rice's version from <i>Vampire Chronicles</i> of &quot;vampires does not change&quot;. On the other hand I know sometimes character need to evolve in game setting. Willpower DOT is also nice middle point for this - very high price for very large life alteration. Also, <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b> paragraph is vague enough to sustain this interpretation<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Willpower Points maybe would do for piercing and exercises, but larger changes need larger commitment - in form of Willpower Dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... you CAN'T regain lost Willpower Dots in 2e. This means you can, at most, change your appearance nine times without basically becoming a mindless drone. The price is far too steep for any change.<br /> <br /> The wording is set up so that, while it doesn't specifically say Willpower Point, it's holding a neon sign and winking. You SPEND Willpower, and spend is only used for Willpower and Vitae points, for dots the wording would be LOSE one.<br /> <br /> Although I would rule that stuff like letting hair and fingernails grow wouldn't cost a point with a successful Resolve+Composure roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T06:14:48-07:00","id":605529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=605518#post605518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But... you CAN'T regain lost Willpower Dots in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er... you can. It costs one experience. Page 83.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T06:53:01-07:00","id":605544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=605529#post605529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er... you can. It costs one experience. Page 83.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... nothing costs a Willpower Dot anymore... Eh, I must just not have enough experience with antagonists to know the ones that can drain Willpower Dots. My mistake. My point about the wording still stands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T07:08:12-07:00","id":605553,"title":"","content":"If I'm not mistaken, your nails grow like 1 centimeter a week. Even if you did use Blush of Life, it would take months to show any sign of progress. Not sure how fast hair grows, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T07:18:36-07:00","id":605558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=605553#post605553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not mistaken, your nails grow like 1 centimeter a week. Even if you did use Blush of Life, it would take months to show any sign of progress. Not sure how fast hair grows, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm... if my nails grew 1cm a week I'd be able to see the difference each day, as I keep mine at roughly 1-2cm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T08:14:57-07:00","id":605609,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It would be millimeters, Nyrufa.<br /> <br /> Hair is 1.25 cm per month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 07-28-2015, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T10:29:52-07:00","id":605684,"title":"","content":"Ok, my two cents.<br /> <br /> You want to let your PCs change a little over time when the players want? That's fair, get 1 Willpower point from them.<br /> <br /> You want to make your PCs be stuck in the same form forever? That's equaly fair, them just DON'T LET THEM.<br /> <br /> You want to make it hard, but not to simply forbid? Argue with them, make them roll hard, limit it in every narrative way you can before actualy letting them do it. And when you let, just get 1 Willpower point from them.<br /> <br /> DON'T ASK FOR DOTS. That's stupid, sorry. Too steep a cost for too little reward, you will just punish your players for having the idea without actualy letting them do the thing.<br /> <br /> This question really have NOTHING to do with if the vampires can or should have signs of growth and change. That's your opinion, and is a valid one, of course. But to actualy make players pay with XP or similar resources for such isn't a good idea. It serves only to charge too much or what IS a minor effect, doesn't matter how hard it should be in-setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T12:03:00-07:00","id":605809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/198676-kindred-and-lasting-physical-changes?p=605544#post605544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But... nothing costs a Willpower Dot anymore... Eh, I must just not have enough experience with antagonists to know the ones that can drain Willpower Dots. My mistake. My point about the wording still stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im pretty sure there's oath and law effects that cost dots, meaning the user's effective willpower pool is permanently reduced accordingly until they run their course or expire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co